<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW2-CI-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW2-CI-004" ;
  triage:title "Test (windows-latest) fails at 1d43815c6: ac8 NullSqliteObservability source-contract test searches for an LF-only cfg(test) marker and misfires on CRLF checkouts" ;
  triage:description "PR #1179 at 1d43815c6, Test (windows-latest): observability::tests::ac8_null_sqlite_observability_is_test_only_in_the_source_contract panics with non-test NullSqliteObservability reference in analyst_query.rs:484. That reference is inside mod tests (cfg(test) at line 457-458), but the test locates the test module with source.find of the literal #[cfg(test)] newline mod tests, which never matches on the Windows runner because the checkout has CRLF line endings (no .gitattributes in the repo). Same cross-platform class as docs/cross-platform-guidelines.md Line Endings. Fix: normalize the source text (strip carriage returns) before the marker search and line indexing, or derive the boundary from lines() rather than a byte search; do not weaken the contract. Run cargo test -p atm-storage-rusqlite and full just lint before pushing." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
